# state: returning   (composed from the kept profile's survey shots; lane.zetaroutes1012)
# Buffy the Vampire Slayer (45410012), Nova, kept profile golden c6b6ec3cb8be.
# Boot and menu cadence read from the survey run z-1791804165-fpsbelow1012-3514899
# (survey.route, HAKUX_ZETA_D24=1); table in docs/lanes/zetaroutes1012/NOTES.md
# section 1. That run's own START/A spam (5s cadence, the same cadence
# buffy.route's first-run menu already uses) produced this screen sequence:
#   052457-booted: title card, "Press START".
#   052502 (START): in-engine cutscene (Giles + fog, ghostly Buffy).
#   052509 (A): main menu (Start Game / Load Game / Options / Extras).
#   052515 (START, Start Game highlighted): "Launch a New Game ... called
#     Buffy 2" / Free Blocks / CONFIRM -- the same confirm screen
#     buffy.route's own comment documents for "Buffy 1" on an empty disk;
#     only the save-slot number differs, because this disk already holds a
#     save. Nothing on the disk is remade or deleted by it.
#   052521 (A): Difficulty select, Easy highlighted.
#   052527 (START): "Summoning" (loading).
#   052532 (A): mission card, "Spanish Mission, Outskirts of Sunnydale,
#     Sunday 11:53PM".
#   052538 (START): live play, canyon, HUD, "Move the R thumbstick..." tip.
# So the menu path below is buffy.route's own (screen-identical on this
# kept-profile disk), and the play loop below is buffy.route's own
# run-and-jump pattern: the survey's late frame 053139-play.png (reached by
# its blind generic loop, ~140s after this route's own mark would land)
# shows Buffy crouched at a ledge under "Run and press B to jump between
# ledges" -- the same tip buffy.route's play loop is built around -- so
# that loop, not the survey's camera-swinging one, is reused here.
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
shot booted
repeat 5 {
    press START
    wait 5
    shot menu-start
    press A
    wait 5
    shot menu-a
}
wait 3
shot pre-mark
mark gameplay               # CHECK: the canyon with the HUD, no PAUSE panel
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    wait 2
    press B
    wait 1.5
    press B
    wait 2
    press A
    wait 0.6
    press X
    wait 1
    axis LX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    wait 2
    press B
    wait 2
    press A
    wait 0.6
    press A
    wait 1
    axis LX min
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    wait 1
    shot play
}
